# Component authoring rules

Every registered component, without exception:

## 1. Spread `{...attributes}` onto the root DOM element

This carries `builder-id`. Missing it is the #1 documented cause of empty
heatmaps — clicks and impressions on that component become invisible.

Pair it with `noWrap: true` in the registration so Builder doesn't also wrap
your output in its own extra div. One root element, one `{...attributes}`
spread — not a double-wrapped div carrying it twice.

```tsx
export function MyComponent({ attributes, ...props }: Props) {
  return <section {...attributes}>...</section>;
}
```
```ts
register("component", { component: MyComponent, name: "MyComponent", noWrap: true, ... });
```

## 2. No interpolated Tailwind classes

`` `text-${align}` `` never compiles — Tailwind's scanner needs the literal
class name string in source to generate it. Use a static lookup map instead:

```ts
const ALIGN_CLASSES: Record<Align, string> = { left: "text-left", center: "text-center" };
// ...
className={ALIGN_CLASSES[align]}
```

Combining multiple *already-resolved* strings from such maps (via template
literal, array join, etc.) is fine — every individual class name is still a
literal Tailwind can see. Only interpolating a raw prop value into a class name
template is the forbidden pattern.

## 3. Real thumbnail + sensible non-lorem defaults

`image` on the registration should be a real, always-available image — an
inline SVG data URI is the simplest way to guarantee that with zero external
dependency (see any of the 3 exemplars in `src/builder-registry.ts` for the
pattern). Every input needs a `defaultValue` real enough that dragging the
component in with zero configuration still looks like something real, not an
empty state or lorem ipsum.

## 4. Sanitize any `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` with DOMPurify

No exceptions. If a component renders HTML from a `richText`/`html` field
(article bodies, `RichText`), it must sanitize before rendering:

```ts
import DOMPurify from "isomorphic-dompurify";
// ...
<div dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: DOMPurify.sanitize(html) }} />
```

## 5. Nothing rendered is hollow

If a visible affordance renders (a cart icon, a form, a button), it does the
real thing. No unmodified copy-pasted example content, no `console.log`
standing in for an action, no static `1 2 3` pretending to be pagination. If
the real thing isn't built yet, don't render the affordance.

## 6. Availability — don't scope by default

Leave `models` unset (available on every model) unless the component is
genuinely narrow-purpose. `Hero`/`Section`/`ProductCard` are deliberately
unscoped because they're needed on `homepage`, `article`, `pdp-section` *and*
page models — scoping to `['page', 'landing-page']` would silently hide them
from contexts that need them. Same caution applies to `requiredPermissions`:
most components should show to everyone (styling access is already gated by
the `editDesigns` role permission at the platform level); reserve
`requiredPermissions` for something genuinely sensitive.

Insert-menu availability (i.e. every `register()` call in
`src/builder-registry.ts`) must run unconditionally — never gate any of it on
`builder.editingModel` or any other condition. That exact gate
(`editingModel === "homepage"`) is what hid 9 components in the old build.

## 7. `canHaveChildren` components receive `children` directly

No Gen-1-style `withChildren()` HOC needed on this SDK — a component
registered with `canHaveChildren: true` just receives a normal `children`
React prop, already rendered. Add a `childRequirements` guardrail if nesting
the component inside itself (or another specific component) would break its
own layout assumptions — see `Section`'s anti-self-nesting rule for the
pattern. Don't restrict children beyond that unless the component is genuinely
narrow-purpose; a general layout wrapper should accept anything.

## 8. One combined registration array

Every component goes into the `CUSTOM_COMPONENTS` array in
`src/builder-registry.ts` — see `.builder/rules/builder-registry.mdc` for why
calling `register("component", ...)` on its own is not enough to render.
